    "text": "Aggregate Product Pollution Conditions Sublimit: $1,000,000"
  },
  {
    "id": "c171",
    "name": "Endorsement 13 — Retroactive Date",
    "text": "Retroactive Date: 11/01/2003"
  },
  {
    "id": "c172",
    "name": "Endorsement 13 — Supplemental Coverage — Products Pollution",
    "text": "SUPPLEMENTAL COVERAGE — PRODUCTS POLLUTION “Claims” and associated “legal defense expense”, in excess of the “self insured retention”, arising out of “product pollution\", provided that the “claim” is first made during the “policy period”. Any such “claim” must be reported to the Insurer, in writing, during the “policy period” or any applicable “extended reporting period”, The coverage afforded pursuant to this Supplemental Coverage only applies to “product pollution” that first commences, in its entirety: 1. During the “policy period” identified in Item 2.a. of the Declarations to this Policy; or, 2. If prior to the “policy period\" identified in Item 2.a. of the Declarations to this Policy, on or after the on or after the Retroactive Date, if any, identified on this Endorsement above."
  },
  {
    "id": "c173",
    "name": "Endorsement 13 — Limits of Liability",
    "text": "Limits of Liability The amount the Insurer shall pay pursuant to this Supplemental Coverage is subject to the Per Product Pollution Condition Sublimit of Liability and Aggregate Product Pollution Sublimit of Liability identified above. These Sublimits are included in, and not in addition to, the Limits of Liability identified in the Declarations to this Policy. Therefore, this Aggregate Product Pollution Conditions Sublimit of Liability shall be the maximum amount the Insurer shall pay for all “claims”, “remediation costs” and associated “legal defense expense” arising out of or related to “product pollution\". However, under no circumstance shall the Insurer be liable to pay any amount in excess of the applicable Limits or Aggregate Limits of Liability identified in the Declarations to this Policy."
  },
  {
    "id": "c174",
    "name": "Endorsement 13 — Products Liability exclusion",
    "text": "Products Liability “Claims”, “remediation costs\" or “legal defense expense” arising out of any goods or products manufactured, sold or distributed by an “insured”. This exclusion shall not apply to “product pollution”, subject to the Sublimits of Liability identified on this Endorsement above and/or the Limits or Aggregate Limits of Liability identified in the Declarations to this Policy."
  },
  {
    "id": "c175",
    "name": "Endorsement 13 — Product Pollution",
    "text": "“Product Pollution” means a “pollution condition” which arises out of the use of a product sold, manufactured, handled, or distributed by the “insured”, provided that such use occurs after the MANU 2 (11/11) © 2011 ited Page 1 of 2 “insured” has relinquished possession of the product. For the purposes of this Policy, products do not include waste products."
  },
  {
    "id": "c176",
    "name": "Endorsement 14 — Trade or Economic Sanctions",
    "text": "This insurance does not apply to the extent that trade or economic sanctions or other laws or regulations prohibit us from providing insurance, including, but not limited to, the payment of claims. All other terms and conditions of the policy remain unchanged."
  },
  {
    "id": "c177",
    "name": "Endorsement 15 — Service of process designee",
    "text": "Information about service of suits upon the company is given below. Service of process of suits against the company may be made upon the following person, or another person the company may designate: Saverio Rocca, Assistant Genera! Counsel ACE USA Companies 436 Walnut Street Philadelphia, PA 19106-3703"
  },
  {
    "id": "c178",
    "name": "Endorsement 15 — Acceptance of service and appearance",
    "text": "The person named above is authorized and directed to accept service of process on the company’s behalf in any action, suit or proceeding instituted against the company. If the insured requests, the company will give the insured a written promise that a general appearance will be entered on the company's behalf if a suit is brought."
  },
  {
    "id": "c179",
    "name": "Endorsement 15 — Submission to Jurisdiction",
    "text": "If the insured requests, the company will submit to the jurisdiction of any court of competent jurisdiction."
  },
  {
    "id": "c180",
    "name": "Endorsement 15 — Acceptance of Court Decision",
    "text": "The company will accept the final decision of that court or any Appellate Court in the event of an appeal."
  },
  {
    "id": "c181",
    "name": "Endorsement 15 — Director of Insurance as agent",
    "text": "The law of some jurisdictions of the United States of America require that the Superintendent, Commissioner or Director of Insurance (or their successor in office) be designated as the company's agent for service of process. In these jurisdictions, the company designates the Director of Insurance as the company's true and lawful attorney upon whom service of process on the company's behalf may be made. The company also authorizes the Director of Insurance to mail process received on the company's behalf to the company person named above."
  },
  {
    "id": "c182",
    "name": "Endorsement 15 — Canadian service of suit",
    "text": "lf the insured is a resident of Canada, the insured may also serve suit upon the company by serving the government official designated by the law of the insured's province."
  },
  {
    "id": "c183",
    "name": "Endorsement 15 — Other-Than-As-Stated Limitation",
    "text": "NOTHING HEREIN CONTAINED SHALL BE HELD TO VARY, ALTER, WAIVE OR EXTEND ANY OF THE TERMS, CONDITIONS, OR LIMITATIONS OF THE POLICY TO WHICH THIS ENDORSEMENT IS ATTACHED OTHER THAN AS ABOVE STATED."
  }
]

